{"name":"Tidal","hex":"#f0f590","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tidal","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to tides."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tidal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tidal (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Tidal is the debut studio album by American singer-songwriter Fiona Apple, released on July 23, 1996, by The WORK Group. Tidal produced three singles: \"Shadowboxer\", \"Sleep to Dream\", and \"Criminal\". The last was the album's most popular single, winning a Grammy Award for Best Female Rock Vocal Performance in 1998. In 2017, Tidal got its first vinyl run as a \"Vinyl Me Please\" exclusive \"Record of the Month\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b5/FionaAppleTidal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tidal_(album)"},{"title":"Tidal (king)","blocks":[{"text":"In the Old Testament, Tidal is a king of Goyim. Septuagint: \"Θαργὰλ βασιλεὺς ἐθνῶν.\" In the Book of Genesis (14:1), he is described as one of the four kings who fought against a group of rebel kings in the Battle of Siddim."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Tempesta_Abraham_Makes_the_Enemies_Flee_Who_Hold_His_Nephew.jpg/330px-Tempesta_Abraham_Makes_the_Enemies_Flee_Who_Hold_His_Nephew.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tidal_(king)"},{"title":"Tidal (service)","blocks":[{"text":"Tidal is a Norwegian-American music streaming service, launched in 2014 by Aspiro and now majority-owned by Block, Inc. Tidal is available in 61 countries and licenses 100 million tracks and 650,000 music videos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Availability_of_Tidal_in_the_World.svg/330px-Availability_of_Tidal_in_the_World.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"htt